    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.62 UBTU-22-255045"
      info        : "The operating system SSH daemon must prevent remote hosts from connecting to the proxy display.

GROUP ID: V-260530
RULE ID: SV-260530r991589

When X11 forwarding is enabled, there may be additional exposure to the server and client displays if the sshd proxy display is configured to listen on the wildcard address. By default, sshd binds the forwarding server to the loopback address and sets the hostname part of the DISPLAY environment variable to localhost. This prevents remote hosts from connecting to the proxy display."
      solution    : "Configure the SSH server to prevent remote hosts from connecting to the proxy display.

Add or modify the following line in the \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config\" file:

X11UseLocalhost yes

Restart the SSH daemon for the changes to take effect:

$ sudo systemctl restart sshd.service"
