    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.86 UBTU-22-431010"
      info        : "The operating system must have the \"apparmor\" package installed.

GROUP ID: V-260556
RULE ID: SV-260556r958702

Control of program execution is a mechanism used to prevent execution of unauthorized programs. Some operating systems may provide a capability that runs counter to the mission or provides users with functionality that exceeds mission requirements. This includes functions and services installed at the operating system level.

Some of the programs, installed by default, may be harmful or may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). Removal of executable programs is not always possible; therefore, establishing a method of preventing program execution is critical to maintaining a secure system baseline.

Methods for complying with this requirement include restricting execution of programs in certain environments, while preventing execution in other environments; or limiting execution of certain program functionality based on organization-defined criteria (e.g., privileges, subnets, sandboxed environments, or roles).

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124, SRG-OS-000368-GPOS-00154, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155"
      solution    : "Install the \"appArmor\" package by using the following command:

$ sudo apt-get install apparmor"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.1,800-171|3.4.7,800-171|3.4.8,800-171r3|03.01.02,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-171r3|03.04.08,800-53|AC-3(4),800-53|CM-7(2),800-53|CM-7(5),800-53r5|AC-3(4),800-53r5|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(5),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CCI|CCI-001774,CCI|CCI-002165,CN-L3|8.1.4.2(f),CN-L3|8.1.4.11(b),CN-L3|8.1.10.2(c),CN-L3|8.5.3.1,CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSCv7|14.6,CSCv8|3.3,CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,CSF2.0|PR.DS-10,CSF2.0|PR.IR-01,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.5.33,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.3,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.9.4.5,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.5.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.6.2,ITSG-33|AC-3(4),ITSG-33|CM-7,ITSG-33|CM-7(2),LEVEL|2A,NESA|T4.2.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.2,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM3,NIAv2|SS15a,NIAv2|SS29,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-260556r958702_rule,STIG-ID|UBTU-22-431010,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,TBA-FIISB|31.1,TBA-FIISB|44.2.2,TBA-FIISB|49.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-260556"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/22168"
      cmd         : "/bin/dpkg -s apparmor | /bin/grep Status: 2>&1"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*Status: install ok installed[\\s]*"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "apparmor.service active"
          cmd         : "/bin/systemctl is-active apparmor.service"
          expect      : "^[\\s]*active$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "apparmor_status profiles are loaded"
